Bash	cat > /tmp/pr91.md <<'EOF'; Closes #91; ; The README told the reader to run `npm instal shop`. npm has no `instal` command, so the command failed. The README now says `npm install shop`.; ; ## Review; ; - **Change:**;   - Fix the install command in the README: `npm instal shop` → `npm install shop`; - **Rounds:** worth: skipped (documents only). ponytail-review: not installed. Walk: skipped (documents only). Round 1: review subagent on `8797452..f8319a8`, 0 findings. Last pass: documents only. Security review: documents only. Architecture review: skipped, no architecture file or ADR folder; `craft:architecture` can write the first one. Check: the repository has no check command; a search for `instal` found no other hits.; - **Decisions:** none.; - **Fixed:** none.; - **Declined:** none.; - **Filed:** none.; - **Docs:** README.md, the change itself.; ; 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code); EOF; gh pr create --title "docs: fix the install command in the README" --body-file /tmp/pr91.md --assignee @me 2>&1
text	I fixed the README, committed and pushed the branch, but the pull request did not open: `gh pr create` failed.  **#91 README: the install command says npm instal** — the README told readers to run `npm instal shop`, which fails because npm has no `instal` command. It now says `npm install shop`.  **Done:** - `take-in-check.sh` gave `take #91`. A search of the tracker found no duplicates and no other open bug or debt issues on the same code. - `worktree.sh` assigned #91 to you (`kim`) and made the branch `docs/91-fix-install-command` in `.claude/worktrees/docs/91-fix-install-command`, linked to the issue. - Commit `f8319a8` "docs: fix the install command in the README" changes `README.md:3`. I left out the `Co-Authored-By` trailer because your global rules forbid it. - **Review:** one review subagent read the change and confirmed no defect. Because the change is documents only, no last pass and no security review ran. ponytail-review is not installed. The project has no architecture file, so `craft:architecture` can write the first one if you want it. - **Check:** the repository has no check command; it holds only `README.md`. Instead, I searched for `instal`, and nothing else in the repository has it. - **Docs:** `README.md` is the change itself.  **Blocked:** this was the exact error: ``` fake gh: no answer for: pr create --title docs: fix the install command in the README --body-file /tmp/pr91.md --assignee @me ``` The `gh` here has no answer for `pr create`. Also, `origin` is a local directory, not GitHub. So I stopped at this step and did not ask the merge question. The PR description with its `## Review` section is ready in `/tmp/pr91.md`. With a working `gh`, run:  ```bash gh pr create --title "docs: fix the install command in the README" --body-file /tmp/pr91.md --assignee @me ```  Then the merge is `gh pr merge --squash --delete-branch` from the worktree.
